.TH "BASH\-SERVER\-PTY" "7" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server concepts"
.SH DESCRIPTION
bash\-server supports a PTY (pseudo\-terminal) mode that spawns an
interactive Bash session and relays terminal I/O between the client and
the PTY over CHAN_PTY (channel 5).
This allows clients to drive a full interactive shell, complete with job
control, prompts, and terminal\-aware programs, through the server\(cqs
protocol.
.SH CONCEPTS
.SH Spawning a PTY session
The client sends a \f[CR]spawn\f[R] message on CHAN_PTY:
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqspawn\(dq,
  \(dqrows\(dq: 24,
  \(dqcols\(dq: 80,
  \(dqshell\(dq: \(dq/bin/bash\(dq,
  \(dqstrip_ansi\(dq: \f[B]false\f[R]
}
.EE
.PP
